# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated art intermediates.
#
# `work/` holds everything the asset pipeline produces *between* an input and a
# finished animation: extracted sprites, the aligned PNG frames per action, the
# review contact sheets, the decoded check images and the browser screenshot.
# None of it is source, and all of it can be regenerated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
work/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built media. NOT tracked, on purpose.
#
# The animations in `assets/anims/` are produced by deforming artwork supplied
# by the person running the build (tools/gen_motion.py), and the sprites it
# deforms are cut from that same supplied artwork. That artwork is third-party
# and copyrighted, so neither the sprites nor anything derived from them can be
# redistributed — which rules out committing the animations.
#
# The repository is therefore code and tools only: it can rebuild a pet from art
# *you* have the right to use, and it ships no art itself. `assets/voice/` is
# untracked for the same reason — it is where a user's own audio lands.
#
# Both directories are recreated by the build, and both keep a .gitkeep so the
# layout stays visible in a fresh clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/anims/*
!assets/anims/.gitkeep
assets/voice/*
!assets/voice/.gitkeep

# Previews and the runtime capture are pictures *of* the character, so they are
# derived from the same supplied artwork and travel with the same restriction.
# They are regenerated by the build (`gen_motion.py` writes the GIFs,
# `verify-browser.mjs` writes the screenshot), which is why dropping them from
# version control costs nothing.
docs/preview/*.gif
docs/screenshot.png

# Local artifacts
*.log
*.local
.env
.env.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Node
node_modules/
.npm/
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
